license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hernandesco/wind-portfolio-tehuantepec"
abstract: "Python code, processed data and results supporting the study of two-level Markowitz portfolio optimization of wind capacity across 20 candidate sites in the Isthmus of Tehuantepec (Oaxaca, Mexico) with wake-risk-aware turbine layout search, an iterative Level 1-Level 2 feedback loop and an NPV/LCOE/CVaR economic evaluation (Acciona AW-77/1500 turbine, 80 m hub height, ERA5 2000-2024). Includes the hourly ERA5-derived capacity-factor, wind-speed and wind-direction series (data/processed), the raw ERA5 10 m wind-speed downloads (data/raw_10m, Zenodo archive only), all result files and the scripts that regenerate every figure. Contains modified Copernicus Climate Change Service information (ERA5, Hersbach et al., 2020), retrieved through the Open-Meteo API."
keywords:
  - "wind energy"
  - "portfolio theory"
  - "Markowitz optimization"
  - "wake effects"
  - "Tehuantepec"
  - "transmission congestion"
  - "diversification"
  - "ERA5"
